    "questionEN": "A platform engineering team wants to share an MCP server for their internal ticketing system across all developers using Claude Code. The server requires an API token unique to each developer. Where should the MCP server be configured, and how should credentials be managed?",
    "question": "Khi nào một hệ thống nên ưu tiên sử dụng MCP transport Server-Sent Events (SSE) thay vì stdio?",
    "optionsEN": [
      "A. Add the server to .mcp.json in the project root with each developer's API token hard-coded in the configuration.",
      "B. Add the server to .mcp.json using ${TICKETING_API_TOKEN} expansion so each developer sets their own token.",
      "C. Have each developer add the server to their personal ~/.claude.json with their API token.",
      "D. Create a shared .env file in the repository with all developer tokens and reference it from .mcp.json."
    ],
    "options": [
      "A. Khi MCP server được lưu trữ từ xa trên một máy chủ đám mây độc lập và phục vụ nhiều client qua mạng HTTP.",
      "B. Khi cần hiệu năng truyền dữ liệu nhị phân tốc độ cao nhất.",
      "C. Khi client chạy trên hệ điều hành Windows.",
      "D. Khi không có kết nối internet."
    ],
    "correct": 1,
    "optionExplanations": [
      "Option A ❌ (SAI): Hard-coding individual tokens in .mcp.json commits credentials to version control, which is a security risk. Each developer has a different token, so a single hard-coded value would not work for the team.",
      "Option B ✅ (ĐÚNG): Project-level .mcp.json is version-controlled and shared, making the server available to everyone. Environment variable expansion keeps individual credentials out of version control while letting each developer authenticate with their own token.",
      "Option C ❌ (SAI): User-level ~/.claude.json is for personal or experimental servers. A team-wide integration should be in project-level .mcp.json so it is version-controlled and consistently available to all developers.",
      "Option D ❌ (SAI): A shared .env file with all developer tokens still commits credentials to version control and creates a single file containing every team member's secrets, compounding the security risk."
    ],
    "rationale": "Project-level .mcp.json is version-controlled and shared with the team, making the server available to everyone. Environment variable expansion keeps individual credentials out of version control whilst allowing each developer to authenticate with their own token.",
    "explanation": "SSE transport được thiết kế cho các kịch bản client-server từ xa qua mạng HTTP, cho phép MCP server chạy tập trung trên hạ tầng đám mây.",
