    "questionEN": "A docs team asks Claude Code to audit documentation coverage across a 500,000-line codebase. After reading 30 files via the Read tool, the conversation is approaching the context limit and earlier tool results will be summarised away by auto-compaction. The agent still needs that earlier information to complete the audit. What is the best strategy?",
    "question": "Nhóm tài liệu yêu cầu Claude Code kiểm toán độ bao phủ tài liệu trên codebase 500.000 dòng. Sau khi đọc 30 file qua tool Read, phiên hội thoại chạm ngưỡng giới hạn context và các kết quả đọc file trước đó sắp bị nén mất bởi auto-compaction. Chiến lược tốt nhất là gì?",
    "optionsEN": [
      "A. Increase the context window size so that all 30+ file contents can be held simultaneously without trimming",
      "B. Have the agent write structured findings to a scratchpad after each file, then read it for the final audit.",
      "C. Process all files in a single Read tool call by passing a glob pattern, so the results arrive in one untrimmed block",
      "D. Run /compact after every 10 files to free up context space for the next batch of file reads"
    ],
    "options": [
      "A. Tăng kích thước context window.",
      "B. Yêu cầu agent ghi các phát hiện có cấu trúc vào một file scratchpad trên đĩa sau mỗi file đọc được, sau đó đọc lại scratchpad để hoàn tất báo cáo kiểm toán cuối cùng.",
      "C. Đọc tất cả các file trong một lệnh Read duy nhất dùng mẫu glob.",
      "D. Chạy /compact sau mỗi 10 file."
    ],
    "correct": 1,
    "optionExplanations": [
      "Option A ❌ (SAI): The context window has a fixed maximum size. A 500,000-line codebase cannot fit entirely in context regardless of configuration. Tool result trimming exists specifically because holding all file contents simultaneously is not feasible.",
      "Option B ✅ (ĐÚNG): A scratchpad file persists on disk and can be re-read at any time, unlike in-context tool results that are trimmed as new results arrive. By extracting and recording the essential findings (not the full file contents) after each file read, the agent decouples its knowledge from context window limits. The final audit reads the compact scratchpad rather than needing all source files in context.",
      "Option C ❌ (SAI): The Read tool reads individual files, not glob patterns. Even if multiple files could be read at once, a single massive result block would itself be trimmed or would consume the entire context budget, preventing the agent from reasoning about the results.",
      "Option D ❌ (SAI): /compact summarises the conversation, which may discard the specific findings from earlier file reads. The problem is preserving information, not just freeing space. Compacting without first persisting findings to disk loses the very data the audit needs."
    ],
    "rationale": "A scratchpad file persists on disk and can be re-read at any time, unlike in-context tool results that are trimmed as new results arrive. By extracting and recording the essential findings (not the full file contents) after each file read, the agent decouples its knowledge from context window limits. The final audit reads the compact scratchpad rather than needing all source files in context.",
    "explanation": "File scratchpad trên ổ đĩa là nơi lưu trữ trạng thái bền vững, cho phép agent đọc lại bất cứ lúc nào mà không sợ bị trôi mất thông tin khi context window bị nén tự động.",
